{"chapter": "algebraization", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DXS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A$", "MATH_0002": "$I$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\mathcal{F}_n)$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\textit{Coh}(X, I\\mathcal{O}_X)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\textit{Coh}(U, I\\mathcal{O}_U)\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\mathcal{F}_n)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{situation-algebraize}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-essential-image-completion}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5f706f8b1b531c68cafbf79f81074a70cf79c63633b6eb4a30f01f114c2fd04c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6d9c5aafffa2ec9e84acdf3e89dbd7907923af397aa70624e27217a3ad34264c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIf in Situation <REF_0001> the ring <MATH_0001> is not\n<MATH_0002>-adically complete, then Lemma <REF_0002>\nsuggests the correct thing is to ask whether <MATH_0003>\nis in the essential image of the restriction functor\n<MATH_0004>\nHowever, we can no longer say that this means <MATH_0005>\nis algebraizable. Thus we introduce the following terminology.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d0b4b17c14ea620a76c9c1a8217af88733d9b6cdbd632900b512c9294220614f", "unit_id": "tag:0DXS:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "algebraization", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0DXS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{F}_n)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{Coh}(U, I\\mathcal{O}_U)$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\mathcal{F}_n)$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\mathcal{G}_n)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\textit{Coh}(X, I\\mathcal{O}_X)$", "MATH_0007": "$U$", "MATH_0008": "$(\\mathcal{F}_n)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{situation-algebraize}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-algebraizable}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5115f4c701f67599e47e89cede3877cdd43447b3b64660ab8e48f3e91384fba5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4915d01699b42b406155d23efde4b5688b60fff4baba69454c28ff00083b2290", "source_text": "In Situation <REF_0001> let <MATH_0001> be an\nobject of <MATH_0002>. We say\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0003> extends to <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if there exists an object\n<MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006> whose restriction\nto <MATH_0007> is isomorphic to <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f911e6fbd2ea2c4d648e7d76db150a3a0ea4858efe3b8d826a7a43cdf93fc64d", "unit_id": "tag:0EIM:statement"}
{"chapter": "algebraization", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DXS", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:daecc1e1867cc1f586d64c8781221a0c14cc6efc127e91473036d502f5d8bbde", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis notion is equivalent to being algebraizable over the completion.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:25f1ee30f395cd82e06338e986a94dcec0247d91e29c8eba8397a58961a118de", "unit_id": "tag:0DXS:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "algebraization", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DXS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{F}_n)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{Coh}(U, I\\mathcal{O}_U)$", "MATH_0003": "$A', I', \\mathfrak a'$", "MATH_0004": "$I$", "MATH_0005": "$A, I, \\mathfrak a$", "MATH_0006": "$X' = \\Spec(A')$", "MATH_0007": "$U' = X' \\setminus V(\\mathfrak a')$", "MATH_0008": "$(\\mathcal{F}_n)$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "MATH_0010": "$(\\mathcal{F}_n)$", "MATH_0011": "$U'$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{O}_{U'}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{situation-algebraize}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-algebraizable}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bb68301d0469022ea17d7963fd86e8f6359656f5d4c00fba3438bcaf580b7521", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:906e738820b4707fffc158b815b981f47784dcc18a83b16d3ee17de9de975459", "source_text": "In Situation <REF_0001> let <MATH_0001> be an\nobject of <MATH_0002>. Let <MATH_0003>\nbe the <MATH_0004>-adic completions of <MATH_0005>. Set <MATH_0006>\nand <MATH_0007>. The following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0008> extends to <MATH_0009>, and\n<STRUCT_0003> the pullback of <MATH_0010> to <MATH_0011> is the completion\nof a coherent <MATH_0012>-module.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ed30f023d3b3520164db0853fc43c00c1f5629c610fef225c770754567c41b0d", "unit_id": "tag:0EIN:statement"}
{"chapter": "algebraization", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DXS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A \\to A'$", "MATH_0002": "$A/I \\to A'/I'$", "MATH_0003": "$X' \\to X$", "MATH_0004": "$Y' \\to Y$", "MATH_0005": "$U' \\to U$", "MATH_0006": "$U' \\cap Y' \\to U \\cap Y$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\textit{Coh}(X', I\\mathcal{O}_{X'}) \\ar[r] &\n\\textit{Coh}(U', I\\mathcal{O}_{U'}) \\\\\n\\textit{Coh}(X, I\\mathcal{O}_X) \\ar[u] \\ar[r] &\n\\textit{Coh}(U, I\\mathcal{O}_U) \\ar[u]\n}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-completion-flat}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-completion-complete}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{coherent-lemma-inverse-systems-pullback-equivalence}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-essential-image-completion}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2531d86bbfa4e8ce79fb3e472553756c160540d4d84aabdb1d449fcec938d30e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:57e2791a9cc9b3c463c104d8a91cd1979846badc4b831f4ec520c03a5a18fd76", "source_text": "Recall that <MATH_0001> is a flat ring map which induces an isomorphism\n<MATH_0002>. See\nAlgebra, Lemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\nThus <MATH_0003> is a\nflat morphism inducing an isomorphism <MATH_0004>. Thus <MATH_0005>\nis a flat morphism which induces an isomorphism <MATH_0006>.\nThis implies that in the commutative diagram\n<MATH_0007>\nthe vertical functors are equivalences. See\nCohomology of Schemes, Lemma\n<REF_0003>.\nThe lemma follows formally from this and the results of\nLemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d1328b0c6a4247c1988befdf00360a5468cd878274bbfd51e56b5a57be458486", "unit_id": "tag:0EIN:proof"}
